.nh
.TH "AEGIS" "1" "May 2026" "aegis 0.1.0-demo" "Aegis Manual"

.SH NAME
aegis-recheck - Re-run the install gate against the current lockfile


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaegis recheck [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
recheck calls /check on every dep in the live lockfile and reports
any that the API now says are blocked (or prompted, with
--fail-on-prompt). Useful after an incident DB update — packages
allowed when installed may now be flagged.

.PP
By default only DIRECT deps are rechecked (matches what the user
explicitly asked for at install time). Pass --all to also scan
transitive deps.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	include transitive deps (default: direct only)

.PP
\fB--fail-on-prompt\fP[=false]
	exit non-zero on prompt verdicts (default: only block fails)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for recheck

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit machine-readable JSON to stdout

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	summary line only (no per-finding detail)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable debug-level structured logging to stderr


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaegis(1)\fP
